(a) Make time the subject of the horizontal equation: $t=\dfrac{x}{30}$.
Substitute into the vertical equation.
$\begin{aligned}y&=20\left(\dfrac{x}{30}\right)-5\left(\dfrac{x}{30}\right)^{2}\\&=\dfrac{2x}{3}-\dfrac{x^{2}}{180}.\end{aligned}$
(b) At launch level, $y=0$.
$\begin{aligned}0&=\dfrac{2x}{3}-\dfrac{x^{2}}{180}\\0&=x\left(\dfrac{2}{3}-\dfrac{x}{180}\right).\end{aligned}$
The roots are $x=0$ and $x=120$, so the range is $120\text{ m}$.
At greatest height, the gradient is zero.
$\begin{aligned}\dfrac{dy}{dx}&=\dfrac{2}{3}-\dfrac{x}{90}\\0&=\dfrac{2}{3}-\dfrac{x}{90}\\x&=60.\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}y(60)&=\dfrac{2}{3}(60)-\dfrac{60^{2}}{180}\\&=20\text{ m}.\end{aligned}$
(c) At $x=0$, the gradient is $\dfrac{2}{3}$, so the angle of projection is $\tan^{-1}\left(\dfrac{2}{3}\right)\approx33.7^{\circ}$ above the horizontal.
At $x=90$:
$\begin{aligned}\left.\dfrac{dy}{dx}\right|_{x=90}&=\dfrac{2}{3}-\dfrac{90}{90}\\&=-\dfrac{1}{3}.\end{aligned}$
The direction is $\tan^{-1}\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)\approx18.4^{\circ}$ below the horizontal.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.05cm,y=0.1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{pathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (-5,0)--(132,0) node[right] {$x$ (m)};
\draw[->,black] (0,-3)--(0,28) node[above] {$y$ (m)};
\draw[thick,pathblue,domain=0:120,samples=80] plot (\x,{2*\x/3-(\x)*(\x)/180});
\fill[black] (60,20) circle (1.2pt);
\path (60,20) node[above] {$(60,20)$};
\fill[black] (90,15) circle (1.2pt);
\path (90,15) node[above right] {$P(90,15)$};
\draw[dashed,black] (75,20)--(108,9);
\path (108,9) node[right] {tangent at $P$};
\path (120,0) node[below] {$120$};
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
A ball is launched from a platform $15\text{ m}$ above the ground with initial velocity $10\mathbf{i}+10\mathbf{j}$ metres per second. Take the launch point as the origin, rightwards and upwards as positive, and $g=10\text{ m/s}^{2}$.
(a) Find the Cartesian equation of its path.
(b) Find how far from the platform's base it lands and its direction at impact, to 1 d.p.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (-0.8,-1.5)--(5,-1.5);
\draw[black] (-0.8,-1.5)--(-0.8,0)--(0,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(4.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-1.7)--(0,1.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[->,black,thick] (0,0)--(1,1) node[above right] {$10\mathbf{i}+10\mathbf{j}$};
\path (0,0) node[above left] {$O$};
\draw[<->,black] (-1.2,0)--(-1.2,-1.5) node[midway,left] {$15\text{ m}$};
\path (3,-1.5) node[below] {ground};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
A projectile launched from the origin follows $y=\dfrac{4}{3}x-\dfrac{1}{72}x^{2}$, where $x$ and $y$ are in metres.
The point $P$ on the path is shown below.
Find the direction of motion at $P$, where $x=60$, to 1 d.p.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$ (m)}, ylabel={$y$ (m)}, xmin=-10, xmax=112, ymin=-5, ymax=40, width=10cm, height=7cm, samples=100, clip=false, xtick={0,20,40,60,80,100}, ytick={0,10,20,30}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:96] {4*x/3 - x*x/72};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(60,30)};
\node[above right] at (axis cs:60,30) {$P$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

